# Implementation Plan – Phase 5: Backend Foundation (Revised for Iranian Market)

This plan outlines the design and implementation details for Phase 5 of the Leitner Learning Platform. We will build the server-side infrastructure using **.NET 8 LTS (ASP.NET Core)**, establishing database schemas, OTP/JWT authentication, user profile management, event bus system, and off-server backup replication, fully customized for domestic Iranian cloud services.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Domestic Service Integrations:**
> - **SMS Gateway:** We will integrate **Kavenegar** as the primary SMS provider (supporting tokenized verification message templates) and provide adapters for **Faraz SMS** and **SMS.ir** as fallbacks.
> - **Object Storage Backup:** We will configure the S3 storage client (using standard AWSSDK.S3) with custom endpoints pointing to domestic S3-compatible providers (specifically **ArvanCloud** or **ParsPack**).
> - **Self-Hosted CAPTCHA Integration:** To mitigate bot spam without relying on unstable Google reCAPTCHA, we will build a self-hosted visual/math CAPTCHA generator endpoint as part of the security foundation.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Schema Source of Truth:**
> We have a predefined SQL schema at [V1__Initial_Schema.sql](file:///e:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/deployment/db/migrations/V1__Initial_Schema.sql). To ensure strict alignment and avoid duplicating SQL migrations as EF Core migrations, we will use **DbUp** inside the C# backend to execute these raw SQL files on startup. EF Core will then map to the resulting tables.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Replication Fallback:**
> The off-server backup replication is triggered immediately upon user registration or purchase changes via an Event Bus. If domestic S3 credentials are not configured, it will log a warning and save JSON backups locally under a `/backups/` directory within the workspace to avoid runtime crashes during local development.

